.TH NETIFY-FLOW-EXPRESSIONS 7
.SH NAME
netify-flow-expressions \- Netify Flow Expression Engine Syntax
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Netify Flow Expression engine provides a powerful way to filter and classify network traffic based on flow metadata and deep-packet inspection (DPI) results. It supports two syntax modes: \fBCompact Syntax\fR for simple application, protocol, and category matching, and \fBStandard Syntax\fR for complex logical expressions.
.SH COMPACT SYNTAX
Compact syntax is a shorthand for matching flows based on application or protocol tags and categories.
.TP
\fBai:\fR\fITAG\fR
Match by application tag (e.g., \fBai:facebook\fR).
.TP
\fBac:\fR\fITAG\fR
Match by application category tag (e.g., \fBac:social-media\fR).
.TP
\fBpi:\fR\fITAG\fR
Match by protocol tag (e.g., \fBpi:tls\fR).
.TP
\fBpc:\fR\fITAG\fR
Match by protocol category tag (e.g., \fBpc:web\fR).
.SH STANDARD SYNTAX
Standard syntax allows for complex logic, multiple attributes, and comparison operators.
.SS Operators
.TP
\fBComparison\fR
\fB==\fR (equal), \fB!=\fR (not equal), \fB>\fR (greater than), \fB>=\fR (greater than or equal), \fB<\fR (less than), \fB<=\fR (less than or equal).
.TP
\fBBoolean\fR
\fB&&\fR or \fBand\fR (logical AND), \fB||\fR or \fBor\fR (logical OR), \fB!\fR (logical NOT).
.TP
\fBGrouping\fR
Parentheses \fB(\fR \fB)\fR can be used to group expressions and enforce precedence.
.SS Data Types
.TP
\fBAddresses\fR
Supports IPv4, IPv6, CIDR notation, and MAC addresses. Address groups can be referenced using the \fB@\fR prefix (e.g., \fB@iot\fR).
.TP
\fBStrings\fR
String constants should be enclosed in single (\') or double (") quotes.
.TP
\fBRegular Expressions\fR
String comparisons support regular expressions when prefixed with \fBrx:\fR (e.g., \fBdetected_hostname == 'rx:.*google.com'\fR).
.TP
\fBIntegers\fR
Supports decimal and hexadecimal (prefixed with \fB0x\fR) values.
.TP
\fBBooleans\fR
Literal \fBtrue\fR and \fBfalse\fR values.
.SH ATTRIBUTES
The following attributes are available for use in standard expressions, organized by category. Each attribute has an expected data type (e.g., address, string, integer, boolean, hex, mixed, constant).

.SS Application & Protocol
.TP
\fBapp_ip_override\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating if the application IP was overridden.
.TP
\fBapp_proto_twins\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating application and protocol twins.
.TP
\fBapplication\fR (mixed)
The detected application tag or ID. (Aliases: \fBapplication_id\fR, \fBapp\fR, \fBapp_id\fR)
.TP
\fBapplication_category\fR (string)
The detected application category tag. (Alias: \fBapp_category\fR)
.TP
\fBapplication_category_id\fR (integer)
The detected application category ID. (Alias: \fBapp_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBcategory\fR (string)
The detected application category tag in an application, domain, category list, overlay, or network intelligence domain categorization. (Alias: \fBcat\fR)
.TP
\fBcategory_id\fR (integer)
The detected application category ID in an application, domain, category list, overlay, or network intelligence domain categorization. (Alias: \fBcat_id\fR)
.TP
\fBdomain_category\fR (string)
The detected category tag from custom category lists. (Alias: \fBdom_category\fR)
.TP
\fBdomain_category_id\fR (integer)
The detected category ID from custom category lists. (Alias: \fBdom_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBprotocol\fR (mixed)
The detected protocol ID or tag. (Aliases: \fBprotocol_id\fR, \fBproto\fR, \fBproto_id\fR)
.TP
\fBprotocol_category\fR (string)
The detected protocol category tag. (Alias: \fBproto_category\fR)
.TP
\fBprotocol_category_id\fR (integer)
The detected protocol category ID. (Alias: \fBproto_category_id\fR)

.SS Network Metadata
.TP
\fBip\fR (address)
Any IP address (local or other).
.TP
\fBsrc_ip\fR (address)
Source IP address.
.TP
\fBdst_ip\fR (address)
Destination IP address.
.TP
\fBlocal_ip\fR (address)
Local IP address.
.TP
\fBother_ip\fR (address)
Other IP address.
.TP
\fBmac\fR (address)
Any MAC address (local or other).
.TP
\fBsrc_mac\fR (address)
Source MAC address.
.TP
\fBdst_mac\fR (address)
Destination MAC address.
.TP
\fBlocal_mac\fR (address)
Local MAC address.
.TP
\fBother_mac\fR (address)
Other MAC address.
.TP
\fBport\fR (integer)
Any port number (local or other).
.TP
\fBsrc_port\fR (integer)
Source port number.
.TP
\fBdst_port\fR (integer)
Destination port number.
.TP
\fBlocal_port\fR (integer)
Local port number.
.TP
\fBother_port\fR (integer)
Other port number.
.TP
\fBip_protocol\fR (integer)
Internet protocol ID (e.g., 6 for TCP, 17 for UDP).
.TP
\fBip_version\fR (integer)
IP version (Values: 4, 6).
.TP
\fBip_dscp\fR (integer)
Differentiated Services Code Point (DSCP) value.
.TP
\fBip_nat\fR (boolean)
Set if the flow is in the connection tracking table on a WAN (Linux only).
.TP
\fBiface\fR (string)
Network interface name (or index).
.TP
\fBiface_nfq_dst\fR (string)
NFQUEUE destination interface name.
.TP
\fBiface_nfq_src\fR (string)
NFQUEUE source interface name.
.TP
\fBnfq_dst_ifindex\fR (integer)
NFQUEUE destination interface index.
.TP
\fBnfq_src_ifindex\fR (integer)
NFQUEUE source interface index.
.TP
\fBvlan_id\fR (integer)
Virtual LAN (VLAN) ID.
.TP
\fBorigin\fR (constant)
The origin end-point of the flow. (Values: \fBorigin_local\fR, \fBorigin_other\fR, \fBorigin_unknown\fR)
.TP
\fBother_type\fR (constant)
The flow other type. (Values: \fBother_local\fR, \fBother_multicast\fR, \fBother_remote\fR, \fBother_broadcast\fR, \fBother_unknown\fR, \fBother_unsupported\fR, \fBother_error\fR)
.TP
\fBtunnel_type\fR (constant)
Set if encapsulated data (like GTP) is identified. (Values: \fBtunnel_none\fR, \fBtunnel_gtp\fR)

.SS Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) & TLS
.TP
\fBbt_info_hash\fR (string)
BitTorrent info hash.
.TP
\fBdetected_hostname\fR (string)
The detected hostname, extracted from various protocols.
.TP
\fBdetection_complete\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating classification is complete (typically < 32 packets).
.TP
\fBdetection_guessed\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating the protocol was 'guessed' (e.g., via ports) if packet analysis failed.
.TP
\fBdetection_init\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating initial application and/or protocol has been detected.
.TP
\fBdetection_packets\fR (integer)
Number of packets processed during detection.
.TP
\fBdetection_updated\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating flow metadata has been extracted (e.g., TLS info) and application refined.
.TP
\fBdhcp_class_ident\fR (string)
DHCP class identifier.
.TP
\fBdhcp_fingerprint\fR (string)
DHCP fingerprint.
.TP
\fBdns_hostname\fR (string)
Hostname extracted from DNS queries.
.TP
\fBhttp_url\fR (string)
HTTP URL.
.TP
\fBhttp_user_agent\fR (string)
HTTP User-Agent string.
.TP
\fBmdns_domain_name\fR (string)
mDNS domain name.
.TP
\fBndpi_risk_client\fR (integer)
Client risk score or mask.
.TP
\fBndpi_risk_score\fR (integer)
Flow risk score or mask.
.TP
\fBndpi_risk_server\fR (integer)
Server risk score or mask.
.TP
\fBrisks\fR (integer)
Flow risks bitmask.
.TP
\fBsmtp_tls\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating SMTP over TLS.
.TP
\fBsoft_dissector\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating a soft dissector was used for classification.
.TP
\fBssh_client_agent\fR (string)
SSH client agent string.
.TP
\fBssh_server_agent\fR (string)
SSH server agent string.
.TP
\fBstun_mapped\fR (address)
STUN mapped address.
.TP
\fBstun_other\fR (address)
STUN other address.
.TP
\fBstun_peer\fR (address)
STUN peer address.
.TP
\fBstun_relayed\fR (address)
STUN relayed address.
.TP
\fBstun_response\fR (address)
STUN response address.
.TP
\fBtls_alpn\fR (string)
TLS Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN).
.TP
\fBtls_alpn_server\fR (string)
TLS ALPN selected by server.
.TP
\fBtls_cert_fingerprint\fR (string)
TLS certificate fingerprint.
.TP
\fBtls_cipher\fR (hex)
The TLS negotiated cipher. (Alias: \fBssl_cipher\fR)
.TP
\fBtls_ech\fR (hex)
TLS ECH (Encrypted Client Hello) version.
.TP
\fBtls_issuer_dn\fR (string)
TLS certificate issuer distinguished name.
.TP
\fBtls_ja4\fR (string)
JA4 TLS fingerprint or identifier.
.TP
\fBtls_proc_certificate\fR (boolean)
TLS processed certificate flag.
.TP
\fBtls_proc_hello\fR (boolean)
TLS processed hello flag.
.TP
\fBtls_server_cn\fR (string)
TLS server common name.
.TP
\fBtls_subject_dn\fR (string)
TLS certificate subject distinguished name.
.TP
\fBtls_version\fR (hex)
The TLS version (e.g., \fB0x0303\fR for TLS v1.3). (Alias: \fBssl_version\fR)

.SS TCP & Transport Metadata
.TP
\fBtcp_fin_ack\fR (boolean)
TCP FIN ACK flag seen.
.TP
\fBtcp_last_seq\fR (boolean)
TCP last sequence state.
.TP
\fBtcp_resets\fR (integer)
Count of TCP resets.
.TP
\fBtcp_retrans\fR (integer)
Count of TCP retransmissions.
.TP
\fBtcp_seq_errors\fR (integer)
Count of TCP sequence errors.

.SS Flow Statistics & Timing
.TP
\fBdst_bytes\fR (integer)
Bytes sent to the destination.
.TP
\fBdst_packets\fR (integer)
Packets sent to the destination.
.TP
\fBdst_rate\fR (integer)
Flow rate to the destination.
.TP
\fBlocal_bytes\fR (integer)
Bytes sent from local.
.TP
\fBlocal_packets\fR (integer)
Packets sent from local.
.TP
\fBlocal_rate\fR (integer)
Flow rate from local.
.TP
\fBother_bytes\fR (integer)
Bytes sent from other.
.TP
\fBother_packets\fR (integer)
Packets sent from other.
.TP
\fBother_rate\fR (integer)
Flow rate from other.
.TP
\fBsrc_bytes\fR (integer)
Bytes sent from the source.
.TP
\fBsrc_packets\fR (integer)
Packets sent from the source.
.TP
\fBsrc_rate\fR (integer)
Flow rate from the source.
.TP
\fBtotal_bytes\fR (integer)
Total flow bytes.
.TP
\fBtotal_dst_bytes\fR (integer)
Total bytes to destination (including overhead).
.TP
\fBtotal_dst_packets\fR (integer)
Total packets to destination.
.TP
\fBtotal_local_bytes\fR (integer)
Total bytes from local.
.TP
\fBtotal_local_packets\fR (integer)
Total packets from local.
.TP
\fBtotal_other_bytes\fR (integer)
Total bytes from other.
.TP
\fBtotal_other_packets\fR (integer)
Total packets from other.
.TP
\fBtotal_packets\fR (integer)
Total flow packets.
.TP
\fBtotal_src_bytes\fR (integer)
Total bytes from source.
.TP
\fBtotal_src_packets\fR (integer)
Total packets from source.
.TP
\fBts_first_seen\fR (integer)
Flow first seen timestamp (UNIX epoch).
.TP
\fBts_last_seen\fR (integer)
Flow last seen timestamp (UNIX epoch).

.SS Networking Groups & Overlays
.TP
\fBnetwork_category\fR (string)
Network category tag. (Alias: \fBnet_category\fR)
.TP
\fBnetwork_category_id\fR (integer)
Network category ID. (Alias: \fBnet_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBlocal_network_category\fR (string)
Local network category tag. (Alias: \fBlocal_net_category\fR)
.TP
\fBlocal_network_category_id\fR (integer)
Local network category ID. (Alias: \fBlocal_net_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBother_network_category\fR (string)
Other network category tag. (Alias: \fBother_net_category\fR)
.TP
\fBother_network_category_id\fR (integer)
Other network category ID. (Alias: \fBother_net_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBsrc_network_category\fR (string)
Source network category tag. (Alias: \fBsrc_net_category\fR)
.TP
\fBsrc_network_category_id\fR (integer)
Source network category ID. (Alias: \fBsrc_net_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBdst_network_category\fR (string)
Destination network category tag. (Alias: \fBdst_net_category\fR)
.TP
\fBdst_network_category_id\fR (integer)
Destination network category ID. (Alias: \fBdst_net_category_id\fR)
.TP
\fBtag\fR (string)
Custom tag defined in the overlay feature.
.TP
\fBtag_category\fR (string)
Custom tag category defined in the overlay feature.
.TP
\fBtag_category_id\fR (integer)
Custom tag category ID defined in the overlay feature.

.SS Caches & Conntrack
.TP
\fBconntrack_id\fR (integer)
The connection tracking ID. (Alias: \fBct_id\fR)
.TP
\fBconntrack_mark\fR (integer)
The connection tracking mark. (Alias: \fBct_mark\fR)
.TP
\fBct_reply_dst_ip\fR (address)
The connection tracking destination IP.
.TP
\fBct_reply_src_ip\fR (address)
The connection tracking source IP.
.TP
\fBdhc_hit\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating a hit in the DNS hint cache (DHC).
.TP
\fBfhc_hit\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating a hit in the flow hash cache (FHC).

.SS Miscellaneous & Flow State
.TP
\fBexpired\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating the flow has expired.
.TP
\fBexpiring\fR (boolean)
Flag indicating the flow is nearing expiration.
.TP
\fBintel_*\fR (string)
Intel metadata fields with dynamic suffixes (matches tokens starting with \fBintel_\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Match all flows belonging to the 'social-media' category:
.RS
\fBac:social-media\fR
.RE
.PP
Match Netflix or YouTube traffic on port 443:
.RS
\fB(app == 'netflix' || app == 'youtube') && local_port == 443;\fR
.RE
.PP
Match traffic from a specific local network that is NOT using TLS 1.3:
.RS
\fBsrc_ip == 192.168.1.0/24 && tls_version != 0x0303;\fR
.RE
.PP
Match flows where the detected hostname ends with '.org':
.RS
\fBdetected_hostname == 'rx:.*\\.org$';\fR
.RE
